.AVIATION...
(12Z TAFS)
Issued at 419 AM PDT Wed Aug 26 2026

The mid/high clouds moved out of our area and the marine layer
quickly reorganized and made a push inland. IFR/LIFR has developed
for a majority of the terminals with KLVK likely to be the only
site impacted by stratus ceilings through the remainder of the
forecast period.

Vicinity of SFO...A steady fetch of onshore flow channeling
through the Bay Area was interrupted briefly by high clouds
earlier Tuesday night into this morning but has now begun to
increase in coverage. VFR ceilings are expected by mid-morning as
stratus retreats back toward the coastline.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...IFR/LIFR ceilings developed in the wake
of upper level clouds, after is seemed possible stratus might not
fill in. Coverage is still not as extensive as normally seen at
this time, with VFR expected by mid to late morning. IFR/LIFR
ceilings aren`t expected to return until around sunset.

